<!--
Starter template for a project CLAUDE.md (or AGENTS.md). HTML comments like this one are
stripped before Claude Code loads the file, so use them for notes to human maintainers.

Rules for filling it in (from the Claude Code memory and best-practices docs):
- Only write what the agent can't learn by reading the repo, or would waste time rediscovering.
- Concrete and checkable: "Run `pytest -q tests/`" not "test your changes".
- Short: well under 200 lines. Move procedures to skills and path-specific rules to .claude/rules/.
- A rule with zero exceptions ("never edit migrations/") belongs in a hook or deny rule too.
- Add a line when you've corrected the same thing twice. Delete lines that no longer earn their place.
Delete every line in angle brackets and every section you have nothing real to say in.
-->
